{"id": "tea:domsum-rabye:ch.3.chinese", "source": "src:domsum-rabye", "location": {"ref": "ch.3.chinese"}, "paraphrase": "The Mahāmudrā of the present day and the Great Perfection of the Chinese tradition differ only in name — 'descending from above' and 'ascending from below', 'simultaneous' and 'gradual' — not in meaning.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["dispute"], "teachers": ["tch:sakya-pandita", "tch:moheyan"], "disputes": ["dsp:sutra-mahamudra", "dsp:sudden-or-gradual"], "notes": "Chapter-level ref; the comparison is with the teaching attributed to Hwashang (Moheyan) at the Samye debate.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:domsum-rabye:ch.3.karpo-chigtub", "source": "src:domsum-rabye", "location": {"ref": "ch.3.karpo-chigtub"}, "paraphrase": "A fool's meditation on Mahāmudrā usually becomes a cause for rebirth as an animal; if not, one is born in the formless realm, or else falls into the cessation of the śrāvakas; the 'white self-sufficient remedy' (a single realisation said to suffice alone) is not the Buddha's teaching.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["dispute", "karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:sakya-pandita"], "disputes": ["dsp:sutra-mahamudra"], "obstacles": ["obs:blank-meditation"], "notes": "Chapter-level ref; wording recalled.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:domsum-rabye:ch.3.mahamudra", "source": "src:domsum-rabye", "location": {"ref": "ch.3.mahamudra"}, "paraphrase": "The Mahāmudrā taught by the Buddha is the wisdom born of empowerment and the meditative absorption of the two stages; apart from this, the Buddha did not teach any other Mahāmudrā.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["dispute", "practice"], "teachers": ["tch:sakya-pandita"], "terms": ["trm:mahamudra"], "disputes": ["dsp:sutra-mahamudra"], "notes": "Chapter-level ref (the tantric-vows chapter); wording recalled.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:domsum-rabye:structure", "source": "src:domsum-rabye", "location": {"ref": "structure"}, "paraphrase": "The three vows — of individual liberation, of bodhisattvas and of the mantra vehicle — must each be understood and kept according to its own rites and rules; mixing their procedures, or practising rites not found in the scriptures, is not the dharma.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action", "ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:sakya-pandita"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-vows"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
